ReShiki licensing
=================

Original ReShiki code and documentation are licensed, at your option, under
either the MIT License (LICENSE-MIT) or the Apache License, Version 2.0
(LICENSE-APACHE). The SPDX expression for this choice is:

    MIT OR Apache-2.0

Third-party material is excluded from this dual-license grant. Code, data,
and other material copied, ported, adapted, or bundled from other projects
remain subject to their respective licenses and notices. Translating code
into Rust does not replace those terms. File-specific notices and the
licenses and attribution records in licenses/ and vendor/ take precedence
for that material. See NOTICE for the locations of those records.

Choosing a license for original ReShiki code does not remove obligations
under the licenses of included third-party material. Preserve the applicable
copyright notices, license texts, disclaimers, and attribution records when
redistributing source or binaries.
